Package: netpipe
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: netpipe contributors <dev@netpipe.io>
Installed-Size: 0
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libpcap0.8 (>= 1.10), libssl3 (>= 3.0), zlib1g (>= 1:1.2.0)
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/netpipe/netpipe
Description: Modular stream-processing engine for networking
 netpipe is a high-performance, pipeline-driven packet processing tool and
 embeddable C library. It composes sources, filters, processors, and sinks
 into a processing pipeline that can capture live traffic, read PCAPs,
 decode protocols (Ethernet/IPv4/IPv6/TCP/UDP/HTTP/DNS/TLS), run Lua
 scripts per-packet, and emit results to PCAP-NG, sockets, TAP/TUN, etc.
 .
 This package provides:
   * /usr/bin/netpipe           — the command-line tool
   * /usr/lib/libnetpipe.a      — the static library for embedding
   * /usr/include/netpipe.h     — the public C API
   * /usr/share/man/man1/...    — manpages
   * /usr/share/netpipe/lua/    — bundled Lua scripts (mitigate.lua, test.lua)
 .
 Built against libpcap 1.10.x, OpenSSL 3.x, and bundled Lua 5.4.7.
